N5008 [temp.alias]/2 + [temp.deduct.type] + [temp.variadic]/4-5.  Deducing a
parameter pack through a QUALIFIED alias template (`N::idxseq<J...>`), the
std::index_sequence shape used by std::apply's __apply_impl.  Previously the
alias-expansion branch was restricted to unqualified template-ids (the lookup
used the base name recursively, which for a qualified name found the wrong
symbol and looped -- the libstdc++ regex member-alias shape), so a qualified
alias was never expanded ("found no match").  Fixed by resolving a qualified
alias template-id through its qualifiers (resolve_scope + QUALIFIED lookup) and
restoring the moved scope before re-deducing.  Covers a non-type and a type pack
through a namespaced qualified alias.  Non-vacuous: each assertion is a concrete
function of the deduced pack.
